<p>India and the United Arab Emirates signed defense and energy agreements on Friday during Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s visit to Abu Dhabi, where he met UAE President Sheikh Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan. India’s foreign ministry said the defense framework covers industrial collaboration, advanced technology, training, exercises, maritime security, cyber defense, secure communications and information exchange. The energy agreements include cooperation on India’s strategic petroleum reserves and liquefied petroleum gas supplies. ADNOC said the oil pact could raise its crude storage in India by up to 30 million barrels and explore crude storage in Fujairah as part of India’s strategic reserve. The talks took place as the war involving the United States, Israel and Iran has disrupted Gulf trade and energy flows, including through the Strait of Hormuz. Modi condemned attacks on the UAE, called for safe transit and unimpeded navigation through Hormuz, and said India was ready to support peace efforts in West Asia. After Abu Dhabi, Modi is due to visit the Netherlands, Sweden, Norway and Italy.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/n_qgYZFU37wdr1Gdh5pU3k2SiySmljxr0eEaNf7OMroz_E-XTVUcyB7Bvq5YqxKWj3LR3uPK-1zEmLlyOpdBdA8T_LmSEOdKy3nQReZ5u_o1' alt='President of the United Arab Emirates Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan meets Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi during an official visit reception in Abu Dhabi on May 15, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Investment package: The UAE announced about $5 billion in investment commitments tied to Indian infrastructure, RBL Bank and Samman Capital.</li><li>Maritime projects: The agreements include a memorandum on setting up a ship repair cluster at Vadinar and cooperation to build ship-repair skills for India’s maritime workforce.</li><li>Computing deal: India’s C-DAC and Emirati technology company G42 agreed on a supercomputer cluster, according to Indian and regional reports.</li><li>Ceremonial welcome: UAE military aircraft escorted Modi’s plane as it entered Emirati airspace before an official reception in Abu Dhabi.</li></ul><blockquote>India’s scale and growth trajectory make it one of the defining energy markets of our time. As demand accelerates alongside a rapidly expanding population, the strength of the UAE India energy partnership becomes ever more critical - Sultan Ahmed Al Jaber</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Indian government: Modi thanked Sheikh Mohamed for looking after the Indian community in the UAE during what he described as challenging times. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/india-ready-to-support-middle-east-peace-efforts-pm-modi-to-uae-president-11501755#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>UAE leadership: The Emirati readout said the two leaders reviewed cooperation under the Comprehensive Strategic Partnership and the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement, including the economy, investment, energy, space, food security, technology and artificial intelligence. (<a href='https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20260515-india-uae-sign-pacts-to-boost-ties-including-in-defense-as-modi-begins-multi-nation-tour/'>Middle East Monitor</a>)</li><li>Energy analysts: Experts cited by IndiaTimes described the petroleum reserve and LPG memorandums of understanding as long-term energy-security measures for India and said the Iran war showed why strategic reserves were important. (<a href='https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/pm-modis-uae-visit-how-india-energy-security-will-benefit-from-agreements-on-strategic-petroleum-reserves-lpg-explained/articleshow/131122104.cms'>IndiaTimes</a>)</li><li>UAE Minister Reem Al Hashimy: Before the visit, the UAE minister of state for international cooperation described Modi as a key figure of friendship and said the relationship was &quot;growing from strength to strength.&quot; (<a href='https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2026/05/14/modi-visit-shows-uae-india-ties-growing-from-strength-to-st